<title>USA: Correctional Services stake cut by group.</title>
<headline>Correctional Services stake cut by group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group including New York-based Zweig-DiMenna said it reduced its stake in Correctional Services Corp to about 5.3 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions included the sale of 79,600 shares between July 16 and July 22 at prices ranging from $12.25 to $12.625 a share.</p>
<p>The Sarasota, Fla.-based company provides staffing services to prisons.</p>
